# Port-Based Persistence

Source of truth: `docs/architecture/persistence.md`.

## Placement

| Artifact | Location |
|----------|----------|
| Repository ports + tokens (`USER_REPOSITORY`, …) | `packages/domain/<context>/ports` |
| Domain errors | `packages/domain/<context>/errors` |
| Domain models | `packages/domain/<context>` |
| TypeORM entities + mappers + repo impls | `packages/infrastructure/postgres/src/contexts/<context>` |
| Migrations (global) | `packages/infrastructure/postgres/src/kernel/migrations` |
| Migration CLI | `packages/infrastructure/postgres/src/kernel/migration-cli` |
| `DataSource` manager + factory + runner | `packages/infrastructure/postgres/src/kernel/data-source` |
| Adapter-internal DI tokens (`DATA_SOURCE`, `POSTGRES_CONFIG`) | `packages/infrastructure/postgres/src/kernel/tokens.ts` |
| Port DI tokens (`UNIT_OF_WORK`, `TENANT_CONTEXT`, `CLOCK`, …) | colocated with the port (`domain` / `platform`) |
| `UnitOfWork` port | `packages/platform` |
| `UnitOfWork` impl (`TypeormUnitOfWork` + ALS) | `packages/infrastructure/postgres/src/kernel/persistence` |
| `AuditableEntity`, `VersionedEntity`, `ChildCollectionWriter` | `packages/infrastructure/postgres/src/kernel/persistence` |
| `TenantContext` impl (`AlsTenantContext`) | `packages/infrastructure/postgres/src/kernel/tenant-context` |
| In-memory fakes | `packages/application/src/testing` |

Export repository classes from `@b2b-saas-starter-kit/postgres`. Do **not** export TypeORM entities or mappers. `postgres:migration:generate` is a draft — review SQL and register the class in `postgres-migrations.ts` before `migration:run`.

## Separate Models + Mappers

```typescript
// domain — pure
export interface TenantRepository {
  findById(id: TenantId): Promise<Tenant | null>
  save(tenant: Tenant): Promise<void>
}

// infrastructure/postgres — TypeORM entity (never exported as domain)
@Entity('tenants')
export class TenantEntity extends AuditableEntity {
  @PrimaryColumn('uuid') id!: string
  @Column() name!: string
  @Column() status!: string
}

// mapper
export const TenantMapper = {
  toDomain(e: TenantEntity): Tenant { /* … */ },
  toEntity(t: Tenant): TenantEntity { /* … */ },
}
```

## Unit of Work

```typescript
// platform
export interface UnitOfWork {
  run<T>(work: () => Promise<T>): Promise<T>
}

// application
await this.uow.run(async () => {
  await this.tenants.save(tenant)
  await this.memberships.save(ownerMembership)
})
```

Do **not** put `EntityManager` on domain port signatures. Do **not** use `@nestjs/typeorm` (`InjectRepository`); bind `DATA_SOURCE` from `DataSourceManager`.

## Tenant-Aware Repositories

Tenant-owned repos extend `TenantAwareRepository` (ambient `TenantContext`). See `multi-tenancy.mdc`.

## Audit & Version Columns

Every entity extends `AuditableEntity`; versioned parent aggregates extend `VersionedEntity`. Child-collection saves use `ChildCollectionWriter` inside `uow.run()`. See `audit-and-versioning.mdc`.

## Cross-Context Data

- FKs only **within** a context
- Across contexts: store branded IDs (`userId`, `tenantId`, `roleId`) — no cross-context FKs/joins
- TypeORM relations only inside `src/contexts/<context>/`; cross-context links are uuid columns, never `@ManyToOne` to another context's entity

## Anti-Patterns

```typescript
// ❌ Port leaking TypeORM
export interface TenantRepository {
  getRepo(): Repository<TenantEntity>
}

// ❌ Domain model = TypeORM entity
@Entity('tenants')
export class Tenant { /* domain methods */ }

// ❌ Application importing EntityManager / contracts DTOs
```
